 - [ ] **PREVIEW-003**: When concurrent requests miss the cache for the same preview key, the system SHALL return 202 with the same job ticket and a two-second retry interval while one shared render job is pending.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-004**: When admitting a completed preview would exceed 12 GiB of cached JPEG data, the system SHALL evict entries before admission so the cache remains within that limit.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-005**: When a render job fails, the system SHALL release its deduplication entry so a later request can enqueue a new job.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-006**: When a completed sheet is admitted to the preview cache, the system SHALL place it in the first-use queue (the queue holding sheets not yet requested since admission).
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-007**: When admitting a sheet would push the first-use queue beyond its configured share of the 12 GiB budget, the system SHALL evict first-use-queue entries oldest-first until the queue fits within its share.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-008**: When a request is served as a 200 response from a sheet in the first-use queue, the system SHALL promote that sheet to the reuse queue (the queue holding sheets re-requested after admission).
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-009**: When a promotion would push the reuse queue beyond its share of the 12 GiB budget, the system SHALL evict reuse-queue entries least-recently-reused first until the queue fits within its share.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-010**: When a request is served as a 200 response from a sheet in the reuse queue, the system SHALL mark that sheet most recently reused.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-011**: The system SHALL keep the first-use queue's share of the 12 GiB budget configurable, defaulting to one quarter of the budget, with the reuse queue holding the remainder.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-012**: When a request arrives for a sheet whose cache entry was previously evicted, the system SHALL treat it as a first use, with no retained history influencing cache placement.
